@spec sonority_spec  src=tests/specs/sonority_spec.lua  loc=1401  cases=49
@exercises tuning (tuning), sonority (sonority)
@surface   tuning.derive, tuning.moves, sonority.score, sonority.cost, sonority.strands, sonority.seats, sonority.onsets, sonority.walk, sonority.spellings, sonority.relax, sonority.springCost, sonority.springs, sonority.search, sonority.solveToPoints

# Intent
  Pins the box score of design/adaptive-tuning.md § What "in tune" means: the
  5-limit column of § Choosing the target chooses the theory, its identity with
  the Tenney height of the sonority's lcm/gcd, and the two invariances that let
  the model hold no reference pitch.
  
  Pins the walk of § The model too: which strands are current at each onset,
  distinctness by step-class, the bass as the class a released chord leaves
  behind it, and the class still sounding that the last n struck have dropped.
  
  Pins the objective the solve minimises: the box summed over the walk's
  sonorities, and the pull counted once per strand (§ Harmonic lock).
  
  Pins the solve of § Solving it: that the DP returns the exact minimum of that
  objective, held against exhaustive enumeration; that a strand held across a
  chord change bends the harmony to it (§ The strand); and the two guards.
  
  Pins the pull's scale on the calibration C7 (§ Harmonic lock): the crossing
  from the otonal seventh to the Pythagorean, and what resolving the chord to
  F–A–C does to that trade (§ The model).
  
  Pins the springs of design/adaptive-springs.md § The model: a spelling read
  off as the displacement gaps at which its pairs sound pure, nearest-octave,
  from the seats of the strands its members name.
  
  Pins the objective those springs stand in (§ The model): stiffness ×
  mistuning² per spring and strength × displacement² per strand, the mistuning
  in cents over fifty and the pull over the window half the displacement lies
  in. The box is no part of it, being a constant in the displacements.
  
  Pins the relaxation that minimises it (§ The model): the sweep's answer on a
  pair whose optimum is a closed form, a strand the springs press to its window
  edge, and a comma loop whose residue no displacement can make slack.
  
  Pins the terms the walk relaxes on (§ The solve): a warm start that buys the
  sweep its speed and not its answer, and a held strand standing as data at the
  displacement it carries while its neighbours settle around it.
  
  Pins the beam that chooses the spellings (§ The candidates): a join admitted
  within two half-windows of the member's own seat, a member no move reaches
  standing alone, a full enumeration the beam of twelve is checked against, and
  the cut running within a waiting set so a deferral crowds no spelling out.
  
  Pins the terms the walk takes from the notation (§ The solve): the seat and the
  window a strand is written under, which onsets a member may wait through, and
  that everything a sonority reads of a member is indexed at its strand.
  
  Pins the walk itself (§ The solve): an answer held against an exhaustive search
  over the same spelling lists, a cap of one taking the greedy road, and a strand
  that has stopped standing at the cents the walk left it.

# Helpers
  @fn near(actual, expected, why)  @ 56-59
      -- The doc's figures are given to 2dp.
  @fn spring(sp, i, j, delta, why)  @ 62-66
      -- A spring pinned whole: which strands it ties, and the gap at which they sound pure.
  @fn evenWindows(count)  @ 69-73
      -- Windows of a 12-EDO notation: fifty cents to the step either side of each strand.
  @fn allFree(count)  @ 76-80
      -- The relaxation's original terms: every strand free, and standing where it was written.
  @fn nameless(cents)  @ 84-86
  @fn gcd(a, b)  @ 132
  @fn lcm(a, b)  @ 133
  @fn tenneyOfSpan(odd)  @ 137-147
      -- Tenney height of the set's lcm over its gcd, taken as rationals: the integers
      -- the coords reach the same number without ever forming.
  @fn shifted(coordSet, prime, by)  @ 150-158
      -- Every coord of the set moved by `by` on one axis, absent exponents included.
  @fn event(ppq, pitch, endppq)  @ 161-163
      -- A note as the command hands it over, which the grouping holds by reference.
  @fn pitchClass(note)  @ 166
      -- The pitch class, which is what a step-class comes to under an octave notation.
  @fn strand(class, notes)  @ 171-177
      -- A strand as the walk reads it: notes given as { ppq, pitch, endppq }, under
      -- the step-class they share. The shortlist is the solve's business rather than
      -- the walk's, so these carry none.
  @fn struck(over, list)  @ 181-187
      -- Strands of one note each, given as { class, ppq, pitch }, every note `over`
      -- long so that it is released where the next strikes.
  @fn placed(class, notes, candidates)  @ 191-195
      -- A strand as the solver reads it: the walk's shape with a shortlist of
      -- candidates, each carrying the coords it would take and its strain.
  @fn fixed(over, list)  @ 200-208
      -- Strands of one note and one candidate, given as { class, ppq, pitch, coords,
      -- strain } and `over` long, with the choice that takes each strand's only
      -- candidate.
  @fn strainOf(num, den, step)  @ 212-214
      -- The strain of a ratio written on a 12-EDO step: its distance from that step
      -- as a fraction of the 50¢ half-window.
  @fn triads(cStrain, dStrain)  @ 225-232
      -- C major then D major, disjoint in class: at n=3 each onset stands alone, and
      -- at n=5 the second sonority holds two classes of the first as well.
  @fn classesAt(strands, sonorityAt)  @ 234-238
  @fn exactly(actual, expected, why)  @ 241-244
      -- The DP is exact, so its answer is held to the enumeration's to the bit.
  @fn nearly(actual, expected, why)  @ 247-250
      -- The solve's own figures are worked further out than the doc's two places.
  @fn scoreAt(strands, choice, sonorityAt)  @ 254-260
      -- What one sonority of the walk scores under a choice, so a passage can be read
      -- chord by chord rather than as its total.
  @fn everyChoice(strands, fn)  @ 263-276
      -- Every choice vector over the strands' shortlists, in odometer order.
  @fn bruteMinimum(strands, n, strength)  @ 278-285
  @fn laidOut(list)  @ 296-300
      -- Strands given as { class, {{ppq,pitch,endppq},..} }, each taking threeWays.
  @fn dorian(dSpans)  @ 345-356
  @fn fromDiamond(class, ppq, pitch, step)  @ 373-379
      -- Each chord is released where the next strikes, a bar of 960 later.
  @fn seventh()  @ 383-388
      -- The written C7, every note taking what its own window holds. The seventh is
      -- strand 4, its candidates 7/4, 16/9 and 9/5 in that order.
  @fn resolving()  @ 391-397
      -- The same chord resolving to F–A–C a bar later.
  @fn fromSparse(class, ppq, pitch, endppq)  @ 411-418
  @fn underRun(endppq)  @ 423-430
      -- A B♭ struck first and released at `endppq`, under a run of five classes the
      -- target fixes: nothing the run transmits says how to read the B♭, so only its
      -- own release decides whether it stands in the sonorities behind it.
  @fn progression(bars)  @ 434-442
      -- A chord to the bar, each released where the next strikes: the passage the walk of
      -- design/adaptive-springs.md § The solve is taken over.
  @fn termsOf(strands, n, moves)  @ 446-453
      -- What the notation and the target hand the walk: an onset per sonority and a spelling
      -- list apiece, at the beam width and the stiffness the figures below are taken under.
  @fn settledFrom(answer, window, strength, stiffness)  @ 457-463
      -- The winner settled by one joint relaxation, which is where the frozen past gives back
      -- what it held along the way; the walk's own cost stands above this until then.
  @fn bruteSpelled(lists, window, strength, stiffness)  @ 468-492
      -- Every combination of the spelling lists, each relaxed cold with every strand free: the
      -- search the walk is held against, in the odometer order everyChoice takes, so that an
      -- exact tie falls to the same combination the walk's own tie-break keeps.

# Cases
  @case 'the 5-limit column of the theory table'  [pure]  @ 501-506
  @case 'the score is the Tenney height of the sonority's octave-free lcm/gcd'  [pure]  @ 510-517
  @case 'the score is blind to where the sonority sits'  [pure]  @ 521-527
  @case 'a repeated member and an octave doubling cost nothing'  [pure]  @ 531-538
  @case 'springs: a spelled major triad, by hand'  [pure]  @ 542-551
  @case 'springs: deviations reduce to the nearest octave, and name strands'  [pure]  @ 555-564
  @case 'springs: a lone member holds no spring'  [pure]  @ 568-571
  @case 'springs: the objective sums the springs and the pull'  [pure]  @ 575-593
  @case 'springs: displacements realising the spelling leave every spring slack'  [pure]  @ 597-611
  @case 'springs: the pull is charged over the window half it lies in'  [pure]  @ 615-624
  @case 'relax: a pair settles where the hand solution puts it'  [pure]  @ 628-638
  @case 'relax: the springs press a strand to its window edge'  [pure]  @ 642-654
  @case 'relax: a comma loop spreads its residue across the springs'  [pure]  @ 658-691
  @case 'relax: a warm start settles where the cold one did'  [pure]  @ 695-711
  @case 'relax: a held strand stands where it was put, and the rest settle around it'  [pure]  @ 715-741
  @case 'spellings: a major triad comes back spelled as the theory table has it'  [pure]  @ 745-758
  @case 'spellings: a bare tritone has nothing to say'  [pure]  @ 762-780
  @case 'spellings: the reach is two half-windows of the member that joins'  [pure]  @ 784-796
  @case 'spellings: a rolled minor defers rather than state what the chord has not'  [pure]  @ 800-817
  @case 'spellings: a width of infinity is the enumeration the beam is checked against'  [pure]  @ 821-835
  @case 'spellings: the cut runs within a waiting set, not across them'  [pure]  @ 839-856
  @case 'spellings: seats, windows and waits are read at the strand a member names'  [pure]  @ 860-876
  @case 'seats: the notation gives each strand its step and the reach either side'  [pure]  @ 880-896
  @case 'onsets: a member waits while an onset it sounds through is still to come'  [pure]  @ 900-916
  @case 'onsets: a member held by recency has stopped, so it is joined to and does not wait'  [pure]  @ 920-934
  @case 'search: the walk returns what an exhaustive search over its spelling lists returns'  [pure]  @ 938-959
  @case 'search: carrying one answer takes the greedy road'  [pure]  @ 963-978
  @case 'search: a strand that has stopped stands where the walk left it'  [pure]  @ 982-1008
  @case 'strands: a class chains through its overlaps and splits where they stop'  [pure]  @ 1012-1029
  @case 'strands: classes never share one, and the order does not follow the input'  [pure]  @ 1033-1046
  @case 'a block chord and an arpeggio of it hand back the same set'  [pure]  @ 1050-1062
  @case 'at n one above the arity consecutive sonorities still overlap'  [pure]  @ 1066-1080
  @case 'a repeated note and an octave doubling each spend one entry'  [pure]  @ 1084-1099
  @case 'a later strand of a class replaces the earlier one'  [pure]  @ 1103-1115
  @case 'a class still sounding stands where the last n struck have dropped it'  [pure]  @ 1119-1132
  @case 'the box is summed over the walk rather than over the onsets'  [pure]  @ 1136-1141
  @case 'the pull is the strength times the square of a strand's strain'  [pure]  @ 1145-1150
  @case 'the pull is counted once per strand however many notes write it'  [pure]  @ 1154-1167
  @case 'the C7's two sevenths cross at a pull of 0.95'  [pure]  @ 1171-1193
  @case 'the solve is the minimum exhaustive enumeration finds'  [pure]  @ 1197-1209
  @case 'a shortlist of one is fixed and still contributes its coords'  [pure]  @ 1213-1234
  @case 'a held strand bends the harmony to it'  [pure]  @ 1238-1260
  @case 'behind a run of fixed classes the answer hangs on the hold'  [pure]  @ 1264-1270
  @case 'the C7 sounding alone crosses at a pull of 0.95'  [pure]  @ 1274-1296
  @case 'the rest of the chord stands still, and the third seventh is dominated'  [pure]  @ 1300-1314
  @case 'resolving to F–A–C the seventh takes the Pythagorean under any pull'  [pure]  @ 1318-1336
  @case 'at n one above the arity the resolution reads the seventh chord's bass alone'  [pure]  @ 1340-1358
  @case 'an exact tie goes to the first candidate rather than to table order'  [pure]  @ 1362-1382
  @case 'an empty shortlist and an unaffordable solve are both refused'  [pure]  @ 1386-1399

